The bloody struggle will end an absolute slavery to America or ruined to Britain by the loss of her colonies. So welcome back to The Rest is History. Top flipper enthusiast and defender of slavery, Benjamin Franklin, is still, hoping that he can somehow bridge the gap between Parliament in London and the militant separatists in New England. So it's December 1772 and he has been leaked. He's been given some letters. They've been written by the governor of Massachusetts, Thomas Hutchinson. So Tom, tell me about these letters.
