that the British government is pursuing a hard line, not because the British despise the Americans as, you know, colonials, but because they are receiving terrible advice from people like Hutchinson. In other words, if they can just be educated, then the British will start behaving well and stop demanding taxes. But the whole thing, you know, this whole wheeves goes terribly wrong because, you know, this is an example of how Franklin doesn't recognise what's going on now in Boston,
英国政府采取强硬路线，不是因为英国人鄙视美国人，你知道，作为殖民地人，而是因为他们从像哈钦森这样的人那里收到了糟糕的建议。换句话说，如果他们能被教育，那么英国人就会开始表现良好，停止要求税收。但整件事，你知道，整个诡计出了大问题，因为，你知道，这是一个例子，说明富兰克林没有意识到波士顿现在正在发生什么，

