independence. He wants to kind of, you know, apply all his prestige and status to the cause of, declaring independence. So on the 5th of July, which is two and a half weeks after Bunkers Hill in Boston, a very kind of bloody battle, the olive branch petition is formally adopted by Congress. So they still haven't given up. They still want to give the British one last chance. And Franklin had voted for it, but he wanted to indicate to everybody in America that he didn't really back it.
独立的人。他想，你知道，运用他所有的声望和地位来支持宣布独立的事业。所以7月5日，也就是波士顿邦克山战役（一场非常血腥的战斗）两周半后，橄榄枝请愿书被国会正式采纳。所以他们仍然没有放弃。他们仍然想给英国最后一次机会。富兰克林投了赞成票，但他想向美国的每个人表明他并不真正支持它。

